Finding: {"title":"PUT /checkride-history/:id lets any authenticated user directly set feeBilled and invoiceId, bypassing the actual billing flow","severity":"HIGH","area":"Checkride fee billing integrity","files":["src/server/routes/routes-checkrides.ts:111-150","src/server/routes/routes-checkrides.ts:2149-2339"],"detail":"The general-purpose checkride history update route (PUT /locations/:locationId/checkride-history/:id) is gated only by requireAuth() (any authenticated school user, not requireAdmin()). Its zod schema (checkrideHistoryUpdateSchema, lines 146-148) accepts examinerFee, feeBilled, and invoiceId directly in the body, and the handler writes them verbatim to the DB (lines 2321-2329) with no validation that an actual invoice with that id exists, that the fee was computed correctly, or that any of the dedicated billing logic (createCheckrideInvoice, settleInvoiceByPaymentPreference, audit logging) ran. This sits alongside three purpose-built endpoints (/bill, /student-signoff, /override-signoff) that DO perform real invoice creation, payment settlement, and audit trail — but this generic PUT lets any of those safeguards be skipped entirely. The frontend (checkride-queue.tsx saveExaminerFee) only ever sends {examinerFee}, confirming feeBilled/invoiceId via PUT is unused-but-reachable surface, not a deliberate feature.","impact":"Any authenticated non-admin user at the school (e.g., an instructor account) could mark a checkride fee as 'billed' with a fabricated invoiceId without any invoice or payment ever being created, hiding an unpaid fee from the Billing Queue (pending-signoff/unbilled lists filter on feeBilled=false) — or conversely, corrupt a real billed record by resetting examinerFee/feeBilled, breaking the record's audit trail and student balance.","recommendation":"Remove examinerFee/feeBilled/invoiceId from the general PUT schema (or require requireAdmin() plus dedicated validation matching the /bill flow), and route all fee-state transitions exclusively through /bill, /student-signoff, and /override-signoff.","confidence":"high"}
confirmed=true only if the defect genuinely exists. If misread → verdict="false-positive". If real but wrong severity → set correctedSeverity. If real but underspecified → verdict="needs-detail" (kept). Return JSON per the schema.

